{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The length of the hypotenuse of a right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> , and the radius of the inscribed circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \nThe ratio of the area of the circle to the area of the triangle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e45c028e5c96e171363a5c845940d2371606f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi r}{h+2r}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{\\pi r}{h+r}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\pi}{2h+r}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{\\pi r^2}{r^2+h^2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"617\" height=\"40\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e5247650c5040309690323b27391e1a96792eed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = A$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the inradius, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the semiperimeter, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the area, we have that the ratio of the area of the circle to the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f6113a4e33c926cdb54ba833215d64024a585889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi r^2}{rs} = \\frac{\\pi r}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" />. Now we try to express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Denote the points where the incircle meets the triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe66bac8ca833d3cfc06cb888d714143ac95106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X,Y,Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the incenter, and denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f17857f2d515198402426f8a17f82c59404f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = AY = z, BX = BZ = y, CY = CZ = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"365\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/1813143dd583c904be52742e0f775caacf46d62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XOZB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a square (tangents are perpendicular to radius), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850eeb0f9b330bf716d25e32f8a25d011c29d511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = BX = BZ = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />. The perimeter can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278c97a66e196e467ceda948440a47dcafcaa08b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, so the semiperimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/786294ba81c75be655bda0e12c983b0ef8919a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. The hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b40f7c6edbd386b316e02fe9f6c014ce06f8060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AY+CY = z+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a4612ef4ac46c6da05b7d06f807612dff8141855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = x+y+z = (z+x)+y = h+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"286\" height=\"20\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9c9c99d4e7cf2482e4a0ded7dfd961292057029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{\\pi r}{h+r}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"92\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1979 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a>